## Read versus reproduce

The current Paper B definitions and relevant figures, historical manuscript remainder, central formal theorem files, source code, raw outputs and corrections were inspected. Primary proofs for the candidate centers were read, not inferred solely from abstracts or summaries. All files were inventoried and archives were opened; this is **not** a claim of line-by-line review of every one of the hundreds of historical files. Historical signed C8/C16 material is retained as history, not silently certified.

The five source snapshots are supplied artifacts. `computation/fresh_logs/` contains actual session logs. `computation/fresh_data/` is a capture of selected output directories in rerun copies: because those copies initially contained supplied data, only stages explicitly listed as completed in the experiment registry certify regenerated outputs. This distinction prevents inherited files, especially old status summaries, from becoming fresh evidence merely by being copied.

One aggregate audit driver was interrupted; its log is retained. The required audit stages and historical test suites were subsequently executed separately. The interrupted driver is never counted as a successful full run.

## Authority when claims conflict

Paper B fixes CM/LM semantics. The final audit and its corrected proofs supersede the older quantum handoff; the adversarial and capability results strengthen the audit where a proof supports the strengthening. The bridge is an extension with extra scalar and measurement contracts, not a reinterpretation of Paper B. Raw benchmark rows support only their recorded comparisons. External literature governs priority, not mathematical validity established by an explicit proof.
